      "body": "`ActiveFrontier::clear` only resets `len`, leaving previously-pushed entries intact. Because the type derives `PartialEq`/`Eq` (and `Debug`), stale data in the unused tail can make two logically-empty frontiers compare unequal and show confusing debug output after `clear()`.\n\nConsider zeroing the previously-used prefix when clearing so the struct’s derived traits reflect the logical state.",
